––– comment –––
Elasticsearch-compatible HTTP endpoints must enforce the same table
permissions as native SQL and JSON endpoints.
––– block: ../base/start-searchd-with-auth –––
––– comment –––
Prepare three synthetic tables; the test user can read only esauth_allowed.
––– input –––
MYSQL_PWD=adminpass mysql -uadmin -h0 -P9306 -e "CREATE TABLE esauth_allowed(body text);"
––– output –––
––– input –––
MYSQL_PWD=adminpass mysql -uadmin -h0 -P9306 -e "CREATE TABLE esauth_private(body text);"
––– output –––
––– input –––
MYSQL_PWD=adminpass mysql -uadmin -h0 -P9306 -e "CREATE TABLE esauth_drop(body text);"
––– output –––
––– input –––
MYSQL_PWD=adminpass mysql -uadmin -h0 -P9306 -e "INSERT INTO esauth_allowed(id,body) VALUES(1,'public');"
––– output –––
––– input –––
MYSQL_PWD=adminpass mysql -uadmin -h0 -P9306 -e "INSERT INTO esauth_private(id,body) VALUES(2,'private');"
––– output –––
––– input –––
MYSQL_PWD=adminpass mysql -uadmin -h0 -P9306 -e "CREATE USER 'esauth_reader' IDENTIFIED BY 'readerpass123';" >/dev/null
––– output –––
––– input –––
MYSQL_PWD=adminpass mysql -uadmin -h0 -P9306 -e "GRANT read ON 'esauth_allowed' TO 'esauth_reader';"
––– output –––
––– comment –––
Ensure that the tables actually exist before checking authorization.
––– input –––
MYSQL_PWD=adminpass mysql -uadmin -h0 -P9306 -N -e "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM esauth_allowed;"
––– output –––
1
––– input –––
MYSQL_PWD=adminpass mysql -uadmin -h0 -P9306 -N -e "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM esauth_private;"
––– output –––
1
––– input –––
MYSQL_PWD=adminpass mysql -uadmin -h0 -P9306 -N -e "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM esauth_drop;"
––– output –––
0
––– comment –––
Native JSON and Elasticsearch search agree on access control.
––– input –––
curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -u esauth_reader:readerpass123 -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"table":"esauth_private","query":{"match_all":{}}}' http://127.0.0.1:9308/search
––– output –––
403
––– input –––
curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -u esauth_reader:readerpass123 -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"query":{"match_all":{}}}' http://127.0.0.1:9308/esauth_allowed/_search
––– output –––
200
––– input –––
curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -u esauth_reader:readerpass123 -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"query":{"match_all":{}}}' http://127.0.0.1:9308/esauth_private/_search
––– output –––
403
––– comment –––
The request body may override the URL index. Wildcard and comma-separated
indices must authorize every resolved table.
––– input –––
curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -u esauth_reader:readerpass123 -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"table":"esauth_private","query":{"match_all":{}}}' http://127.0.0.1:9308/esauth_allowed/_search
––– output –––
403
––– input –––
curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -u esauth_reader:readerpass123 -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"query":{"match_all":{}}}' http://127.0.0.1:9308/esauth_allowed,esauth_private/_search
––– output –––
403
––– input –––
curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -u esauth_reader:readerpass123 -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"query":{"match_all":{}}}' http://127.0.0.1:9308/esauth_*/_search
––– output –––
403
––– comment –––
Count and multi-search must enforce read permissions for every target.
––– input –––
curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -u esauth_reader:readerpass123 -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"query":{"match_all":{}}}' http://127.0.0.1:9308/esauth_private/_count
––– output –––
403
––– input –––
printf '%s\n' '{"index":"esauth_allowed"}' '{"query":{"match_all":{}}}' | curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -u esauth_reader:readerpass123 -H 'Content-Type: application/x-ndjson' --data-binary @- http://127.0.0.1:9308/_msearch
––– output –––
200
––– input –––
printf '%s\n' '{"index":"esauth_allowed"}' '{"query":{"match_all":{}}}' '{"index":"esauth_private"}' '{"query":{"match_all":{}}}' | curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -u esauth_reader:readerpass123 -H 'Content-Type: application/x-ndjson' --data-binary @- http://127.0.0.1:9308/_msearch
––– output –––
403
––– input –––
printf '%s\n' '{"index":"esauth_private"}' '{"query":{"match_all":{}}}' | curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -u esauth_reader:readerpass123 -H 'Content-Type: application/x-ndjson' --data-binary @- http://127.0.0.1:9308/esauth_allowed/_msearch
––– output –––
403
––– comment –––
The ES index-count shortcut must not list private table names or document counts.
––– input –––
curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -u esauth_reader:readerpass123 -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"size":0,"aggs":{"indices":{"terms":{"field":"_index"}}}}' http://127.0.0.1:9308/_all/_search
––– output –––
403
––– comment –––
Document deletes require WRITE; table creation and deletion require SCHEMA.
––– input –––
curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -u esauth_reader:readerpass123 -X DELETE http://127.0.0.1:9308/esauth_private/_doc/2
––– output –––
403
––– input –––
curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -u esauth_reader:readerpass123 -X PUT -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"mappings":{"properties":{"title":{"type":"text"}}}}' http://127.0.0.1:9308/esauth_created
––– output –––
403
––– input –––
curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -u esauth_reader:readerpass123 -X DELETE http://127.0.0.1:9308/esauth_drop
––– output –––
403
––– input –––
if MYSQL_PWD=adminpass mysql -uadmin -h0 -P9306 -N -e "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM esauth_created" >/dev/null 2>&1; then echo 'created unexpectedly'; else echo 'creation denied'; fi
––– output –––
creation denied
––– input –––
if MYSQL_PWD=adminpass mysql -uadmin -h0 -P9306 -N -e "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM esauth_drop" >/dev/null 2>&1; then echo 'drop denied'; else echo 'deleted unexpectedly'; fi
––– output –––
drop denied
––– comment –––
Metadata and refresh operations cannot reveal unauthorized tables.
––– input –––
curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -u esauth_reader:readerpass123 http://127.0.0.1:9308/esauth_private/_mapping
––– output –––
403
––– input –––
curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -u esauth_reader:readerpass123 http://127.0.0.1:9308/esauth_allowed/_ilm/explain
––– output –––
403
––– input –––
curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -u esauth_reader:readerpass123 -X POST http://127.0.0.1:9308/esauth_private/_refresh
––– output –––
403
––– comment –––
Authorized admin retains ES-compatible schema operations.
––– input –––
curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -u admin:adminpass -X PUT -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"mappings":{"properties":{"title":{"type":"text"}}}}' http://127.0.0.1:9308/esauth_created
––– output –––
200
––– input –––
if MYSQL_PWD=adminpass mysql -uadmin -h0 -P9306 -N -e "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM esauth_created" >/dev/null 2>&1; then echo 'created'; else echo 'missing'; fi
––– output –––
created
––– input –––
curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -u admin:adminpass -X DELETE http://127.0.0.1:9308/esauth_created
––– output –––
200
––– comment –––
Cleanup.
––– input –––
MYSQL_PWD=adminpass mysql -uadmin -h0 -P9306 -e "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS esauth_allowed;"
––– output –––
––– input –––
MYSQL_PWD=adminpass mysql -uadmin -h0 -P9306 -e "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS esauth_private;"
––– output –––
––– input –––
MYSQL_PWD=adminpass mysql -uadmin -h0 -P9306 -e "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS esauth_drop;"
––– output –––
––– input –––
MYSQL_PWD=adminpass mysql -uadmin -h0 -P9306 -e "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS esauth_created;"
––– output –––
––– input –––
MYSQL_PWD=adminpass mysql -uadmin -h0 -P9306 -e "DROP USER 'esauth_reader';"
––– output –––
